# Receipts split by KIND, and the line is evidence vs. decision.
#
# EVIDENCE is session-local, not repo history: each file describes one PR at
# one moment, is worthless once the moment passes, and is re-derivable at will.
# Three shapes are ignored --
#   pr-*.json                 readiness, quoted in a merge claim and checked by the merge hook
#   loop-round-check-*.json   rounds counted from a snapshot for the budget guard
#   loop-round-check-*.claim  the atomic single-use claim on one such receipt
#
# DECISIONS (loop-budget-*.json, loop-extension-*.json) are committed instead.
# They are taken once and bind afterwards, and they MUST survive the container
# or tripwire 2 can never fire: an ephemeral extension record means a loop that
# already spent its one self-serve adjudication is offered the self-serve
# tripwire again by the next session, forever.
#
# Named shapes rather than ignoring the directory and re-including exceptions,
# because git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded --
# written that way the negations read correctly and do nothing. The cost is
# that a NEW evidence shape must be added here; the benefit is that the rule
# actually works. A new file in this directory that is evidence belongs on
# this list.
#
# The round COUNT is deliberately evidence. It was a committed file in this
# mechanism's first design, and that is precisely what failed: a cache of state
# GitHub already holds, which drifted from it four different ways in one
# evening.
#
# This lives in the directory it governs rather than in the repo root so that
# it is an ordinary synced file — one copy in the handbook, carried to every
# consumer. Patterns are relative to this directory.
pr-*.json
loop-round-check-*.json
# Matches BOTH claim shapes: the original `<check>.json.claim`, and the
# per-generation `<check>.json.<nonce>.claim` the guard writes now that the
# claim is keyed to the receipt's nonce (`claimPath` = `${checkPath(pr)}.${nonce}.claim`).
# The narrower `*.json.claim` pattern stopped matching the moment the nonce
# was added -- a silent coupling break that showed up only as an untracked
# file -- so the pattern is written to cover the whole family rather than one
# spelling of it.
loop-round-check-*.claim
